  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating SkillBridge App**\n\nI\'m starting with a comprehensive outline for the SkillBridge web application. Focusing on core functionality, I\'m identifying key modules based on the brand guidelines and screenshots. My initial step involves a thorough skill check, assessing the available capabilities for this project.\n\n\n**Assessing Potential Skill Usage**\n\nI\'m now evaluating potential skills. Image generation might have limited use given the user\'s focus on hotlinking or existing assets. The Gemini API could be integrated for AI-driven features like resume summarization, though this is secondary to core screen development and features. My top priority remains replicating the provided screens and establishing key workflows.\n\n\n**Analyzing Screen Functionality**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the provided screenshots, concentrating on functional elements. Specifically, I\'m examining the \"Market\" screen, paying attention to the header, filter tabs, banner, and the \"Latest Opportunities\" section, including its sort feature and card designs, noting key details. I\'m focusing on UI elements like buttons and modals, with an eye toward implementing dark/light mode toggle and ensuring theme consistency across the app.\n\n\n**Detailing Project Requirements**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the \"Market\" screen elements, specifically the opportunity cards. I\'m focusing on replicating the visual design of a sample card, specifically the \"\342\232\241 82% Match\" badge. I need to figure out its size and color, along with the price tag, description text, and tags. Then I need to determine the format of the footer details. I also need to focus on the `Apply Now` button and how to render it. I\'m now transitioning to the \"Project Details\" screen, looking at the hierarchy of elements like the back arrow, title, and the three-dot menu, as well as the layout of its specific data.\n\n\n**Defining Screen Elements**\n\nI\'m now examining several more screens in detail. I\'m focusing on the \"Recommended Students\" screen for UMKM, breaking down each candidate card\'s structure, including avatar, name, match percentage, and relevant skills. I\'m noting the actions like \"View Profile\" and \"Invite Student\", focusing on their visual design. Also, I\'m examining a \"My Projects\" screen for students, which include tabs for \"Pending,\" \"Active,\" and \"Completed\" projects.\n\n\n**Enumerating Specific UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"My Requests\" screen elements and formatting, including status tabs for \"Active,\" \"Pending,\" etc., and project cards which show status badges, titles, assigned students, progress, and action icons. I\'ve also noted that the bottom navigation will need a Home tab pill to render for the UI. I have been dissecting cards for features such as their color attributes.\n\n\n**Outlining Current Screen Structure**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"My Requests\" screen. I\'m noting specific action icons such as the eye, edit, and chat icons rendered as blue circles. I\'m examining each card\'s components, including the badge \"Active,\" the project title \"E-commerce Integration,\" the assigned student \"Michael Wong,\" progress (80%), and last update (1 day ago). I\'m also planning the bottom navigation bar with \"Home,\" \"Market,\" \"Chat,\" and \"Profile.\" I\'ve also identified key screens such as the splash screen with the logo, which includes the blue graduation cap icon and \"SkillBridge\" text. I\'m focusing on the landing page, noting the top bar elements, the main heading \"Bridge Your Skills, Empower Local Businesses,\" and the subtext along with CTA buttons and the badge row, including the illustration.\n\n\n**Defining Additional UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now detailing additional components. I need to include a badge reading \"Project Success Rate 98.5%\" with a green upward chart icon, and I\'m updating the footer navigation to the bottom bar. Also, I\'ve started examining the Register/Sign Up screen with a soft blue/gray gradient background, graduation cap logo, \"Create your account\" heading, role selector cards (Student and UMKM), and form fields for full name, email, password, and confirmation, including their icons. I also need to account for a \"Create Account\" button and the \"Log in\" link. And finally, I\'ve noted the Login/Sign In Screen elements, logo, heading, subtext, and email and password input fields with their icons.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 253262577
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
