  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Initial Requirements**\n\nOkay, I\'m starting by breaking down the file requirements for SkillBridge Adaptive. My focus right now is on that initial landing or hero page. It looks like it\'ll require a header component with specific elements, including a logo, notifications, profile/authentication features, and a prominent badge element.\n\n\n**Defining Landing Page Elements**\n\nI\'ve moved on from the initial requirements and am now focused on fleshing out the SkillBridge Adaptive landing page content. I have a headline (\"Bridge Your Skills, Empower Local Businesses\") with a call-to-action description (\"Get Started ->\", \"Explore Projects\"), and I am visualizing a \"Join 5,000+ Collaborators\" badge with an avatar stack, plus a card illustration for project success.\n\n**Mapping Project Screen Structure**\n\nI\'m now diving into the market/projects screen, thinking through tab structures for project filtering. I am planning a \"Recommended For You\" banner, followed by a sortable list of the latest opportunities. Each project card is being designed with match percentage badges and detailed information like company, price, skills, difficulty, duration, and apply buttons.\n\n\n**Detailing Project Specifics**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the specifics of individual project details, from the perspective of both the UMKM and the students. I\'ve focused on the project cards, defining elements like the Lumina Beans Roastery name, match ratings, a specs grid, project overview and objectives, required skills, and deliverables. I am also considering \"About the UMKM\" with a profile link, and a bottom bar with save and apply actions. Moving onto the UMKM\'s recommended students screen, I have a search bar and filter for matching with students. Student cards will display the student profile and match information, and the ability to view the profile or invite the student. Finally, for the student\'s \"My Projects\" screen, I am envisioning tabs for pending, active, and completed projects.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Current Tasks**\n\nI\'ve been assessing the status of three distinct projects: Urban Threads UI design is 65% complete, Bloom\'s marketing campaign is nearly done at 85%, and LocalRoast\'s data analysis is just getting underway, at 25%. I\'m keeping an eye on their respective deadlines and associated actions. I\'ve also focused on the My Requests screen for UMKM clients, defining filters and cards with associated actions. I\'m now starting to visualize the student dashboard, including a welcome message and key metric displays.\n\n\n**Visualizing Future Screens**\n\nI am now focusing on new screen designs. I\'m imagining a student dashboard with key features, including a list of recent projects with statuses and due dates, as well as a monthly activity visual chart. I\'ve also been considering the admin analytics screen, including an overview title with metric cards for Total Users, Active Projects, and Success Rate, along with platform activity logs and user growth statistics. I\'ve also defined the register and login auth screens. Finally, I\'m conceptualizing interactive modals for project applications and a workspace with simulated chat.\n\n\n**Designing New Modal**\n\nI\'ve been working on new modals, specifically a \"Request/Post Project\" form for UMKM clients. It includes fields for project details, required skills, duration, and budget. Plus, I\'m integrating an AI Match Generator using Gemini, with an endpoint to calculate student-project match scores and generate recommendation rationale based on student profiles and project descriptions. I\'m also planning a role switcher for easy toggling between user views and mode selectors for light/dark and responsive views. Now, I\'m setting up server routes and making sure the Gemini API key is handled correctly.\nI am also setting up branding colors in `src/index.css`!\n\n\n**Defining Style Guidelines**\n\nI\'m now focusing on our style guide in `src/index.css`, starting with primary and secondary colors, surface colors, typography (Inter), rounded corners, and glassmorphic effects using `backdrop-blur-md` and shadow levels. I\'m reviewing Tailwind CSS utility classes for customization. I\'m also planning the application structure, including type definitions, mock data, and the navbar component.\n\n\n**Structuring UI Components**\n\nOkay, I\'m now diving into component-level details, mapping out the UI for the application. I\'m focusing on the bottom navigation bar (`/src/components/BottomNav.tsx`) to ensure a mobile-friendly experience. I am also working on the hero screen (`/src/components/LandingHero.tsx`) with a success badge, along with CTA buttons and statistics. I am continuing to map the design for screens 1-5, in the order described.\n\n\n**Mapping Additional Screens**\n\nI am now visualizing additional screens and components, like a student dashboard (`/components/StudentDashboard.tsx`) with a welcome message, project counts, score, and activity chart, and an admin overview screen (`/src/components/AdminOverview.tsx`) with key metrics. I\'ve also detailed the authentication flows for register and login, and the application workspace with chat, as well as a new create project modal. Plus, I\'ve specified a notification drawer. I\'m taking a look at the server.ts file to see what server endpoints are being used.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 14
      nanos: 950929754
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
