  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing UI Components**\n\nOkay, I\'m now zeroing in on the UI components. I\'m starting by breaking down the header navigation element. I\'m paying close attention to the branding, logo, and search bar implementation, and checking them against our design system and corresponding screenshots. I\'m focusing on `Navbar.tsx`, making sure it\'s accurately defined.\n\n\n**Examining Navigational Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the bell icon and user avatar within the header. I\'m noting the red notification badge and the role badge dropdown implementation for quick role switching. I am also working on screen navigation shortcut tabs, which provide quick access for desktop. My next focus is the mobile bottom navigation bar in `/src/components/BottomNav.tsx`, specifically the active state pills, ensuring they match specified screenshots.\n\n\n**Reviewing Home Page Elements**\n\nI\'m now diving into the home page layout. I\'ve broken it down into sections, starting with the SkillBridge header, including the search and bell icon. I\'m taking a close look at the top category filter chips and the \"Recommended For You\" featured banner, noting the call to action. Next, I am looking at the \"Latest Opportunities\" section and its sorting options, then the cards with specific company details, match scores, and skill tags. I\'m meticulously comparing these details against screenshots. I\'m ready for the next section - ProjectDetails.\n\n\n**Detailing Project Information**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the project details, starting with \"Lumina Beans Roastery.\" I\'m carefully documenting the match pill and subtitle, details grid, and the various project sections. I\'m taking a close look at \"Project Overview\", \"Project Objectives,\" \"REQUIRED SKILLS,\" and \"DELIVERABLES\", noting the styling for each section. Also, I am noting the UMKM information and the bottom sticky bar.\n\n\n**Inspecting Student Projects**\n\nI\'m now focusing on `MyProjectsWorkspace`, specifically screenshot 4, analyzing active student projects. I\'ve noted the \"My Projects\" heading, the filter tabs for pending, active, and completed projects, and the sort/filter dropdown. I\'m taking a close look at the project cards, their details like due dates, completion percentages, and status indicators. I\'m also carefully noting the `Workspace` and `Chat` buttons for each project card, comparing details with corresponding screenshots.\n\n\n**Evaluating Project Displays**\n\nI am now closely evaluating the UMKM project listings, noting the \"Eye,\" \"Edit,\" and \"Chat\" action icons associated with various projects like \"Lumina Beans Roastery\" and others, including the \"Coffee Blend Packaging\" match. I\'m also focusing on the \"+ Create New Request\" button, as the final element of focus.\n\nI\'ve also moved on to the `StudentDashboard`, reviewing screenshot 11. I am noting the welcome header, the active/completed projects metrics, and the portfolio score with the \"Top 5% Student\" badge. Finally, I\'ve noted the recent project listing, their statuses and the monthly activity chart.\n\nI\'m also looking at the `AdminOverview` screen and heading, noting the total users metric.\n\n\n**Assessing Authentication Pages**\n\nI\'m now diving into the authentication flows. I\'ve broken down both the registration and login pages, comparing details like logos, headings, and form fields with screenshots. I\'m noting the clear distinction between student and UMKM roles during registration. I am next analyzing the interactive modals, including `ApplyModal`, `WorkspaceModal`, `ChatModal`, and `AIMatchModal`. I\'m detailing the functionality of each, specifically the integration of the Gemini AI and live chat features.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 25
      nanos: 284624963
    }
