  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing HTML Specifications**\n\nI am now thoroughly reviewing the HTML designs and specifications provided. I\'m focusing on the \"Change Password\" view, specifically the structure, labels, and input fields. I\'m paying close attention to the user requirements for headers, titles, and overall presentation. I am also identifying any potential areas that require special consideration in the implementation, to ensure the prompt is implemented properly.\n\n\n**Defining Password Reset Feature**\n\nI am now focusing on the components of the \"Change Password\" view. I\'m considering the three input fields: current, new, and confirmed password. I am also planning the password strength meter and the visibility toggles to show/hide the password text. I\'m defining the actions, specifically the cancel action, and the save changes action, which will trigger a toast or navigate to a success screen.\n\n\n**Outlining Profile Edit View**\n\nI am now structuring the profile edit view, encompassing avatar management, a profile visibility toggle, and personal information fields like name, headline, and bio with a character counter. I\'m incorporating skills as tags with a delete button and an input field for adding new ones. Finally, I\'ve outlined the \"Cancel\" and \"Save Changes\" action buttons and their navigation.\n\n**Designing Help Center Components**\n\nI am now focusing on the Help Center hub, I\'m integrating a search input within the hero banner. I\'m arranging content into a Bento Grid structure, including FAQ, documentation, support contact, problem reporting, and feedback categories, to ensure ease of navigation for users.\n\n**Composing Success State Display**\n\nI am working on the success state\'s visual elements, I am adding an animated checkmark icon within a glowing green circle. I\'m also planning the heading text and considering any additional, optional elements to convey completion.\n\n\n**Defining Search Functionality**\n\nI\'m now creating the global search feature, starting with the hero header\'s search input and a microphone icon. I am incorporating quick filters for categories. I\'m also planning the recent searches and trending skills sections, and project, student, and category suggestions within a Bento Grid, all for effective search results.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 552870162
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
